@question {{id}} | {{title}}
@template choices.v1
@version 1
@goal {{objective}}
@given {{given}}
@domain L1, L2 and L3 form a student attempt containing an error; later lines may carry an earlier error. The intended operation reaches every column.
@read {{reading_id}}
@step 10 | Which line first fails to apply the row operation to the complete row?
{{choices_1}}
@feedback {{wrong_1_1_id}} | L2 only carries forward the unchanged constant from L1; the omission first occurs in L1.
@feedback {{wrong_1_2_id}} | L3 is a consequence of the incomplete earlier line; inspect L1 before judging later arithmetic.
@after {{after_1}}
@wrong Find the earliest omitted constant or coefficient operation before judging later arithmetic.
@why The first incomplete operation is visible in the constant column: L_1 leaves {{second_2}} unchanged, but the constant must use {{constant_expression}}.
@step 20 | What is the corrected consequence of that first error?
{{choices_2}}
@feedback {{wrong_2_0_id}} | This leaves the old constant {{second_2}} untouched. The complete constant update is {{constant_calculation}}.
@feedback {{wrong_2_1_id}} | This subtracts only one copy of {{first_2}}, although the required multiple is {{k}}. The complete constant update is {{constant_calculation}}.
@after {{after_2}}
@wrong Recalculate the missing operation from the original entries.
@why Recalculate that constant from the original rows: {{constant_calculation}}.
@end
